    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d561-a3">

                <pb facs="0883" n="755" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg755"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No. 396.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Foster to Mr.
                            Elduayen</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">San
                                Ildefonso</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-08-22"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 22,
                        1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your excellency’s note of the 18th instant, in which you communicate
                    to me the resolution taken by your worthy colleague, the minister of ultramar,
                    for the payment of the amount awarded to the owner of the Masonic by his
                    excellency the minister of Italy, by which it is contemplated to shorten the
                    period of six months, within which it was agreed the payment should be made in
                    Washington.</p>
                <p>I will lose no time in making known to my Government the measures proposed to be
                    taken for this purpose, which I have no doubt will be found acceptable to
                    it.</p>
                <p>I improve, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN W. FOSTER.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
